@page "/primitives/timepicker"
@using PINGWorks.SitecoreBlok.BlazorUI.Catalogue.Services
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<ComponentPage Title="TimePicker" Description="A time selection input" Interactivity="ComponentInteractivity.Interactive" ApiElements="@TimePickerElements">

	<InstallationNote>
		<p>The picker renders its panel through the shared Popover infrastructure, so the same setup applies:</p>
		<ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1">
			<li>
				Register the BlazorUI services in <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">Program.cs</code>:
				<CodeViewer Code="@("builder.Services.AddSitecoreBlokUI();")" Language="CodeLanguage.CSharp" ClassName="!mt-2" />
			</li>
			<li>
				Place a single <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;Popovers /&gt;</code> container in your root layout:
				<CodeViewer Code="@("<Popovers @rendermode=\"InteractiveServer\" />")" Language="CodeLanguage.Razor" ClassName="!mt-2" />
			</li>
		</ol>
		<p>The panel's Hour, Minute and Period dropdowns are <code>Select</code>s, which use the same host — so this one requirement covers the whole component.</p>
	</InstallationNote>

	<DivergenceNote>
		<p><strong>Ported to Blok's composite picker on 2026-09-04.</strong> This was a native <code>&lt;input type="time"&gt;</code>, which shared no DOM, no sub-components and no interaction model with Blok. It is now Blok's shape: a trigger button showing the formatted time and a clock icon, opening a popover with Hour, Minute and Period <code>Select</code>s and Clear / Done buttons. The trade is deliberate and worth stating — you lose the browser's native time entry, including the mobile time wheel and free keyboard typing, and gain Blok-matching structure and the AM/PM model.</p>
		<p><strong>The value stays <code>TimeSpan?</code>.</strong> Blok models time as <code>TimeValue &#123; hour, minute, period &#125;</code> — three strings — because TypeScript has no time type. .NET does, and <code>TimeSpan</code> round-trips to the 12-hour parts without loss, so the API keeps it. This is a paradigm translation, not a behavioural difference: the rendered control and everything the user does with it match Blok. It also means the change was not breaking for anyone already bound to <code>TimeSpan?</code>.</p>
		<p><strong>The panel is a separate internal component.</strong> Blok keeps the whole picker in one function. A <code>Popover</code> renders its content through the popover host, and that host does not re-render when the originating component's state changes — so a panel whose dropdowns must reflect the current selection has to own that state itself. <code>TimePickerPanel</code> is that component. It is implementation detail, not a second export to compose.</p>
	</DivergenceNote>

	<ExamplesSection>

		<ComponentExample Title="Default" Code="@("<TimePicker @bind-Value=\"selectedTime\" />")">
			<div class="space-y-4">
				<TimePicker @bind-Value="SelectedTime" />
				<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Selected: <strong>@( SelectedTime is null ? "(none)" : SelectedTime.Value.ToString( @"hh\:mm" ) )</strong></p>
			</div>
		</ComponentExample>

		<ComponentExample Title="Preselected" Code="@("<TimePicker @bind-Value=\"meetingTime\" />")">
			<TimePicker @bind-Value="MeetingTime" />
		</ComponentExample>

		<ComponentExample Title="Custom placeholder and labels" Code="@("<TimePicker @bind-Value=\"reminderTime\"\n            Placeholder=\"When should we remind you?\"\n            HourLabel=\"Hr\"\n            MinuteLabel=\"Min\"\n            DoneText=\"Set reminder\" />")">
			<TimePicker @bind-Value="ReminderTime"
						Placeholder="When should we remind you?"
						HourLabel="Hr"
						MinuteLabel="Min"
						DoneText="Set reminder" />
		</ComponentExample>

		<ComponentExample Title="Disabled" Code="@("<TimePicker Disabled=\"true\" />")">
			<TimePicker Disabled="true" />
		</ComponentExample>

	</ExamplesSection>

</ComponentPage>

@code {
	private TimeSpan? SelectedTime;
	private TimeSpan? MeetingTime = new( 14, 30, 0 );
	private TimeSpan? ReminderTime;

	private static readonly ApiElement[] TimePickerElements =
	[
		new ApiElement(
			Name: "TimePicker",
			Description: "Trigger button plus a popover holding Hour, Minute and Period `Select`s. Two-way bindable via `@bind-Value` to a `TimeSpan?`.",
			Depth: 0,
			Properties:
			[
				new ApiProperty( "Value",                "TimeSpan?",                   false, "Selected time as a 24-hour `TimeSpan`. Null when unset or cleared." ),
				new ApiProperty( "ValueChanged",         "EventCallback<TimeSpan?>",    false, "Fires whenever an Hour, Minute or Period field changes, and when Clear is pressed." ),
				new ApiProperty( "Placeholder",          "string",                      false, "Shown on the trigger until a time is picked. Default: `\"Pick a time\"`." ),
				new ApiProperty( "Disabled",             "bool",                        false, "Disables the trigger so the panel cannot open. Default: `false`." ),
				new ApiProperty( "PanelAriaLabel",       "string",                      false, "Accessible name for the popover, which is a `dialog`. Default: `\"Choose time\"`." ),
				new ApiProperty( "HourLabel",            "string",                      false, "Label above the hour dropdown, and its accessible name. Default: `\"Hour\"`." ),
				new ApiProperty( "MinuteLabel",          "string",                      false, "Label above the minute dropdown, and its accessible name. Default: `\"Minute\"`." ),
				new ApiProperty( "PeriodLabel",          "string",                      false, "Label above the AM/PM dropdown, and its accessible name. Default: `\"Period\"`." ),
				new ApiProperty( "ClearText",            "string",                      false, "Label on the button that clears the value and closes the panel. Default: `\"Clear\"`." ),
				new ApiProperty( "DoneText",             "string",                      false, "Label on the button that closes the panel. Default: `\"Done\"`." ),
				new ApiProperty( "ClassName",            "string?",                     false, "Extra CSS classes appended to the outer wrapper." ),
				new ApiProperty( "AdditionalAttributes", "Dictionary<string, object>?", false, "Captured unmatched attributes, forwarded to the wrapper." ),
			]
		),
	];
}
